hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15743","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ali Abu Ja'far narrated to us, from Rafi' ibn Bishr, he is Abu Bishr al-Sulami, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Soon a fire will emerge from Habs Sayl, moving like the movement of slow camels, moving by day and stopping by night, going in the morning and evening. It will be said: The fire went in the morning, O people, so go in the morning. The fire said midday, O people, so rest at midday. The fire went in the evening, O people, so go in the evening. Whoever it catches, it will consume him."
